# NOBORU PERFORMANCE RULE

Version: 1.0

Priority: HIGH

Status: AUTHORITATIVE

This rule governs runtime performance, loading behavior, bundle discipline, and responsiveness across Noboru.

Every page, route, service call, animation, and data workflow must respect the performance targets defined in architecture.mdc and uiux.mdc.

Performance protects learning flow.

Slow software breaks focus.

⸻

PURPOSE

The purpose of this rule is to ensure:

* Fast initial load on mobile networks
* Near-instant route transitions within the app shell
* User interactions feel immediate
* Animations remain smooth at 60fps
* Core learning flows stay usable offline and under load
* Noboru remains Lighthouse-competitive as features grow

Optimize systems.

Not individual screens in isolation.

⸻

REQUIREMENTS

Targets

From architecture.mdc:

* Initial Load < 2 seconds on representative mobile conditions
* Route Change < 300ms for in-app navigation
* User Action < 100ms perceived response for primary interactions
* Animation 60fps
* Lighthouse score > 90 for core pages where measurable

Scope

* Applies to app routes, feature workflows, API latency, client rendering, and asset delivery
* Core learning paths receive highest priority: lessons, reviews, vocabulary, kanji, grammar

Frontend

* Prefer Server Components where interactivity is not required
* Split client bundles with dynamic import for heavy modules
* Avoid unnecessary re-renders in drill and review loops
* Prefetch only when it improves real navigation paths

Data

* Fetch only required fields
* Paginate large lists
* Cache stable reads where architecture permits
* Offline-first features must not block interaction waiting for network retries

Assets

* Optimize images and media per asset-pipeline and assets.mdc rules
* Lazy-load non-critical visuals
* Never block lesson start on decorative assets

API and Services

* Keep service methods focused to reduce round trips
* Batch reads where appropriate
* Avoid sequential waterfall requests in critical screens

Animations

* Animations must remain smooth and purposeful
* Respect reduced motion
* Do not animate expensive layout properties without need

Measurement

* Profile before large optimizations
* Track regressions on core routes during review

⸻

CODING STANDARDS

React and Next.js

* Minimize client component tree depth on hot paths
* Memoize only when profiling shows benefit
* Stabilize callbacks passed to expensive child trees in review and game loops

Network

* Show optimistic UI only where domain rules allow
* Use skeleton states instead of blocking spinners on full pages when possible

Database

* Index query paths used in due reviews and dashboards
* Avoid unbounded selects in repositories

Lists

* Virtualize long lists where rendering cost is measurable

Monitoring

* Treat performance regressions on core flows as defects, not cosmetic issues

⸻

SUCCESS CRITERIA

Performance work is successful when:

* Core learning screens feel immediate on mobile
* Route transitions remain under target in normal conditions
* Primary actions respond within 100ms perceived latency
* Animations remain smooth during drills and transitions
* Lighthouse remains above 90 on agreed core pages
* Bundle growth is justified by user value
* Offline paths avoid unnecessary network blocking

⸻

FAILURE CRITERIA

Performance quality is degraded when any of the following occur:

* Lesson or review screens wait on decorative assets
* Large client bundles loaded for static pages
* Unindexed queries on hot paths
* Re-render storms during answer submission loops
* Full-page blocking fetches for small UI updates
* Animation jank on primary interactions
* Route changes noticeably lag beyond 300ms in normal conditions
* Performance optimizations that break accessibility or pedagogy

When failure criteria appear, profile core flows before adding more features to the same path.

⸻

EXAMPLES

Correct route performance

Review page loads session shell immediately and streams due items via service call with skeleton cards.

Correct bundle split

Heavy game module dynamically imported only on game routes.

Correct query

Repository selects id, prompt, due_at for review queue instead of full content graph.

Incorrect pattern

Dashboard page client-fetches entire vocabulary table on mount.

Incorrect animation

Continuous bouncing mascot during timed quiz causing layout thrash.

Incorrect API usage

Five sequential service calls on lesson open that could be one composed read.

⸻

ANTI-PATTERNS

Giant client-only pages for mostly static content

Fetching entire datasets for small UI widgets

Unvirtualized thousand-item lists

Synchronous heavy work on main thread during answer grading

Blocking lesson entry on non-critical animations

Premature memoization everywhere without measurement

Performance tuning that hides missing indexes

Optimizing Lighthouse by removing essential instructional content

Adding caching without invalidation strategy on progress mutations

Shipping large unoptimized media on critical paths

END OF performance.mdc
